2  4118397  Kirsty-Tou-Hum-Fem-Neu ascended to demigoddess-hood.  338 [345]

I said to myself a while back that the worst of deciding to do every
class would be the moment when I had only Tourists and Healers left.
I managed Healer a little while back, so that left Tourists as the
final hideous obstacle; however, to my intense surprise, the third
Kirsty-T to enter the Dungeons ascended.

The game got rolling nicely with an armour shop on level 2 - a class
could hardly be better equipped for robbery than Tourists. Conversely,
I didn't get a general store in the main dungeon until DL 15, far too
late to price-ID. I spurned the Mines entrance on DL 2, and then an
altar rolled around on DL 3. The Lady doled out Cleaver straight away,
and I figured I could more than make do with that; Cleaver's
ordinarily not thought much of, but it sure rips through the early
beasties.  A scroll shop on 5 let me ID identify, and another armour
shop gave me a good selection. I used a CoDisplace nearly all game,
carefully avoiding becoming invisible, which worked very well; I also
had GoDex for nearly all the game, but at +0 until after the Castle.

At this point things went a bit awry when I found a +2 elven shield at
the Oracle, which doesn't work so well with Cleaver. Elves had also
supplied me with a decent supply of daggers to replace my dwindling
dart supply. I figured with the shield I'd have a really respectable
negative AC, so I went back up to the altar. Magicbane popped out, and
I'd use it for most of the game. Around now I must have done Sokoban
(getting the BoH), getting poison resistance from an elderly quivering
blob corpse on the top level, eliminating one major YASD worry; I also
got a corpse and telepathy from about the twelfth floating eye I
killed.

Back to the Mines, only to fall for the old trick where you use the
first digging implement you find in a frenzy of eagerness, and it's
cursed. _And_ it was a mattock, so I can't get any HW out of my bag. A
quick trip up to the altar solves that one, and gets me Giantslayer
when I'm actually trying to re-zero my prayer timeout.  I suppose they
can't all be Fire Brand.

Izchak has a magic lamp, which is nice of him. Deep in the Mines I
have a momentary panic when I step on a polytrap, but of course I have
Magicbane so I'm fine - that is, until the vrock round the next corner
summons a buddy and they beat on me. I kill them, but it's close; I
leave a boulder on top of the polytrap to prevent a recurrence.

After getting the luckstone I notice the (cross-aligned) priest is
quite near the stairs, so I dig a few tunnels and then rob the general
store by teleporting out, and flee the level. I figure by the time I
want to donate I'll be able to run rings around the guards.

On DL 9 I kill my first air elemental, and shortly after I find
another magic lamp which becomes GDSM, and now I'm getting pretty
confident. I get crowned, then find another altar on DL 11, where I
make some pools out of a fountain and move my stash. Just then a Xorn
turns up with a bag of tricks, which is certainly nice of him.

The Quest was very generous to me. First a wraith kindly leaves a
corpse on the Home level, which gets me the XL 14 I need to go on the
Quest; then there's a third magic lamp which becomes a SoR; then a
soldier brings along a WoDeath which has some charges left when I take
him down, and the Master of Thieves is dust. Then I have the PYEC, so
I can zap big nasties with wild abandon - as a result, even though I
have emergency genocide in reserve, I'm not too afraid of mind flayers
(the PYEC also grants extrinsic telepathy so you can see them coming).

Robbed a shop on DL 15; got Mojo from an altar on the way up to donate
(and I must have had Vorpy by now, but I don't remember when I got it
- I kept Mojo and Vorpy all game, but didn't really use them much);
had a throne genocide, which went on disenchanters; went back and
cleaned out the deep Mines levels since before I'd just grabbed the
luckstone and legged it. Then I found an altar on 21; I wasn't so
dependent on altars at this stage because I had identify at 0%
failure, but I moved my stash to DL 23.

Medusa and the Castle presented few problems. I went in the back of
the Castle, since then you can search the armour room before tackling
the mob, but there was nothing good there. I tackled the mob anyway,
and the wand was 0:2, but of course I needed no scrolls of charging. I
burned wishes on a magic marker, a HoBrilliance (since I was now using
a lot of spells and didn't need a HoESP), a spellbook of magic mapping
(I didn't want to chance writing it on spec), and a ring of free
action, leaving two wishes in reserve; I already had speed and
levitation boots, and would later find water walking.

Gehennom was mostly plain sailing, but an Archon turned up on a trip
through the Castle to the stash, and summoned a bunch of nasties - I'd
maxed out XL to have plenty of mana and good spell failure chances. I
dealt with them, though, and he left Demonbane - but I decided not to
bother with it. Both Asmodeus and Baalzebub had WoDig which forced me
to chase them down several levels, and Jubilex was full of gremlins to
which I lost my intrinsic telepathy, a minor annoyance. Then I
fumble-fingered and overenchanted my CoDisplace when I found a magic
marker; fortunately I had a spare in my stash.

Rodney's Tower had another SoGeno in, and a magic lamp, but I'd carry
the former with me to the end and got no wish from the latter. Ah
well. On the way up the Tower liches became a nuisance, and I
genocided them with one of my collection of SoGeno. I established a
final cache on level 1 (stuff for the Endgame like SoGD and some holy
water and WoDig, and K-rats) and a secondary cache at Vlad's (just
holy water and food), then went up to the top of the Tower and killed
Rodney.

I wished up an AoR so I could remove my SoR to cast spells, then -
since I wasn't Stealthy, not having got it from my goddess and with my
fingers full of warning and free action - used charm monster to move
through the Sanctum graveyard quickly. Getting through here fast is
amazingly important; if you dawdle, random monster generation makes
the space around the temple very crowded. As I was I just ran around
the priests, kicked in the door, zapped the High Priest with a death
ray, and away I went; unfortunately I'd forgotten to make a cursed
PoGL, but I still escaped quickly because the graveyard was full of my
pets.

The mysterious force was very severe in the deep part of Gehennom, but
I wasn't worried; Magicbane soaked up the curses, I had a vast reserve
of HW and bSoRC (too much, as usual; couldn't carry as much other
stuff as I'd like), and with three WoDeath and the PYEC Rodney was
lucky to last one turn after turning up. I met Yeenoghu in the Valley,
not sure where he came from. Unfortunately it all went a bit
pear-shaped on the Planes.

Firstly, cursed SoGD are not as good as confused, because you can't
see the portal once you get in range! I had to keep an eye open for
monsters disappearing on Water and Air, and automatic searching
helped. Also, I left my BoLev on DL 1, and so had to rely on the three
PoLev I'd brough just in case. This worked OK on Air - actually Air
was very easy, with only one PoFH needing quaffed - but on Water I was
worried about them running out, so donned AoMB and put my BoH in my
oilskin sack. Then I forgot to worry about eels, and an electric eel
blew up my ring of free action, which could have been very bad news on
Astral.

The only plus side on Astral was that, now I didn't have any vital
rings or wands, I could just take off my SoR for charming monsters and
soak up the odd zap, without taking off AoLS for an AoR. This in turn
eased my mind about being paralysed and killed. Since I had a vast
supply of WoDeath zaps I decided to do Famine (centre) -> Pestilence
(right) -> Death (left), especially as I also had cure sickness at 0%.
Famine was tough to get into because of a vast mass of summoning, and
I had to charm monster several times; of course it was the wrong
altar, and I had to struggle out again. However near the exit a
cockatrice turned up, and I quickly turned it into a weapon. This let
me rip into Pestilence in no time at all, but that was wrong as
well. The rubber chicken lasted, so I was off to Death; charmed a
bunch of ants as a screen - I did take a few rounds of combat from
Death, but got her behind me and ran for it, and that was that.

